Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:45:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui: scheduled toasts persist and fire after the
 program has exited

AddToSchedule keeps each scheduled toast under HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\
Notifications\Scheduled (content, delivery time, snooze, tag, group, owner
process). While the scheduling program runs its own worker shows the toast and
updates or removes the entry; for a program that has exited a scheduler host
(rundll32 windows.ui.dll,SgToastScheduler, started by the first AddToSchedule and
by the user's Run key at logon, ending a minute after nothing is left) shows it,
under the program's name, and a click starts the program. A new process of the
same program lists and removes the toasts an earlier one scheduled
(GetScheduledToastNotifications, RemoveFromSchedule).

